---
import Layout from '../../layouts/BlogPost.astro';
---

<Layout
	title="Cuttle Privacy Policy"
	description="Privacy Policy for Cuttle, the desktop editor for ink interactive fiction"
	pubDate={new Date('October 12 2026')}
>
	<h2>Privacy Policy for Cuttle</h2>
	<p><strong>Last Updated:</strong> October 12, 2026</p>

	<h3>Introduction</h3>
	<p>
		Cuttle ("we", "our", or "us") is a desktop application for writing, playing, and debugging
		interactive fiction written in the ink scripting language. We are committed to protecting
		your privacy. This Privacy Policy explains how we handle information when you use Cuttle.
	</p>

	<h3>Information We Collect</h3>
	<p>
		<strong>Cuttle does not collect, store, or transmit any personal data.</strong> There are no
		servers, no accounts, and no analytics. Cuttle does not connect to the internet in the course
		of normal use. We do not:
	</p>
	<ul>
		<li>Collect your name, email address, or any other personal information</li>
		<li>Require you to create an account or sign in</li>
		<li>Track your location</li>
		<li>Access your contacts, photos, microphone, or camera</li>
		<li>Use analytics, crash reporting, or tracking SDKs</li>
		<li>Use third-party advertising networks</li>
		<li>Upload your stories or any part of your files anywhere</li>
		<li>Sell or share data with anyone</li>
	</ul>

	<h3>Your Files</h3>
	<p>
		Cuttle works with plain <code>.ink</code> files on your computer. It reads and writes only
		the files and folders you explicitly choose through the system open and save dialogs. Your
		stories, project files, and any edits you make stay on your device and are never sent to us
		or to anyone else. The app runs in the macOS App Sandbox, which restricts it to the
		locations you have granted access to.
	</p>

	<h3>Local App Data</h3>
	<p>
		To make the app convenient to use, Cuttle keeps a small amount of data on your device: the
		list of projects you have recently opened (so the Recent menu can reopen them), your chosen
		entry file for each project, window size and position, and any runtime state you choose to
		save from the preview panel. This data is stored locally in the app's own support folder and
		never leaves your computer. If you remove the app, this data is removed with it.
	</p>

	<h3>External Links</h3>
	<p>
		The Help menu includes links to the ink website and the "Writing with ink" guide on GitHub.
		Choosing one of these opens the page in your default web browser. Those sites are operated
		by inkle Ltd and GitHub respectively and are governed by their own privacy policies. Cuttle
		itself sends no information to them. A copy of the "Writing with ink" guide is bundled with
		the app so it can be read offline without visiting any website.
	</p>

	<h3>Third-Party Services</h3>
	<p>
		Cuttle does not integrate with any third-party services that collect user data.
	</p>

	<h3>Children's Privacy</h3>
	<p>
		Cuttle does not collect personal information from anyone, including children under 13 years
		of age.
	</p>

	<h3>App Store Information</h3>
	<p>
		When you download Cuttle from the Mac App Store, Apple may collect information according to
		its own privacy policy. We do not receive personally identifiable information from Apple
		beyond aggregated, anonymous download and crash statistics that Apple provides to all
		developers.
	</p>

	<h3>Changes to This Policy</h3>
	<p>
		We may update this Privacy Policy from time to time. Any changes will be reflected on this
		page with an updated "Last Updated" date.
	</p>

	<h3>Contact Us</h3>
	<p>
		If you have any questions about this Privacy Policy, please contact us at:
	</p>
	<p>
		<a href="mailto:evan+cuttle@mightystrong.io">evan+cuttle@mightystrong.io</a>
	</p>
</Layout>
